---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About — EdgeShaping"
  description="About mare interno LLC, the measurement-infrastructure company behind EdgeShaping, the patent-pending AI bot observability framework."
  lang="en"
  path="/about"
  altPath="/ja/about"
>
  <section class="deep" style="padding-top: 160px;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--ai);">About</span>
      <h2 style="color: var(--foam);">An observation tool, built by a measurement company.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        EdgeShaping is developed by mare interno LLC, a Tokyo consultancy specializing in
        measurement infrastructure — server-side GTM, GA4, Consent Mode and CMP implementation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shallow">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 760px;">
      <table class="data reveal">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Product</th><td>EdgeShaping / EdgeShaping Lite — AI bot observability framework</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Patent</th><td>Patent pending — the AHQG Matrix / EdgeShaping system</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Company</th><td>mare interno LLC</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Location</th><td>Kuwano Bldg. 2, 6-23-4 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, Japan</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Focus</th><td>Measurement infrastructure (sGTM / GA4 / Consent Mode / CMP), AI bot observability</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Sales &amp; support</th><td><a href="https://mareinterno.com/" rel="noopener">mareinterno.com</a></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top: 40px; color: var(--ink-soft);">
        Our stance is simple: AI bots are welcome here — but not unobserved. EdgeShaping exists
        not to block them, but to make them visible.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
